problem:
Problem description
- There is one beverage product planned over a finite weekly horizon of $$T$$ periods indexed by $$t \in \mathcal{T} = \{1,\dots,T\}$$.
- For each period $$t$$, the input data include market demand $$d_t$$, production capacity $$u_t$$, and unit production cost $$c_t$$.
- A unit holding cost $$h$$ is incurred for each unit of inventory left after meeting the demand of a period.
- The plan determines the production quantity $$x_t$$ in each period and the ending inventory level $$I_t$$ after demand is satisfied.
- The planning goal is to minimize the total cost over the horizon, consisting of production cost and inventory holding cost.
- Weekly demand must be satisfied on time.
- Production in any period cannot exceed the available production capacity of that period.
- Inventory may be carried from one period to the next, but only nonnegative inventory is allowed.
- Unmet demand is not allowed.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_t$$, the planned production quantity in period $$t$$.
  - $$I_t$$, the inventory remaining at the end of period $$t$$.
  - $$Z$$, the total cost of the plan over all periods.

Input Format
{
  "time_horizon": {
    "symbol": "$$T$$",
    "meaning": "Number of planning periods in the horizon"
  },
  "periods": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T} = \\{1,\\dots,T\\}$$",
    "meaning": "Ordered set of weekly periods"
  },
  "demand": {
    "shape": "array of length $$T$$",
    "symbol": "$$d_t$$",
    "meaning": "Demand in period $$t$$"
  },
  "capacity": {
    "shape": "array of length $$T$$",
    "symbol": "$$u_t$$",
    "meaning": "Maximum producible quantity in period $$t$$"
  },
  "production_cost": {
    "shape": "array of length $$T$$",
    "symbol": "$$c_t$$",
    "meaning": "Unit production cost in period $$t$$"
  },
  "holding_cost": {
    "shape": "scalar",
    "symbol": "$$h$$",
    "meaning": "Unit inventory holding cost charged for leftover inventory in each period"
  },
  "initial_inventory": {
    "shape": "scalar",
    "symbol": "$$I_0$$",
    "meaning": "Inventory available at the start of period $$1$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "production_plan": {
    "shape": "array of length $$T$$",
    "symbol": "$$x_t$$",
    "meaning": "Planned production quantity in period $$t$$"
  },
  "ending_inventory": {
    "shape": "array of length $$T$$",
    "symbol": "$$I_t$$",
    "meaning": "Inventory remaining at the end of period $$t$$"
  },
  "total_cost": {
    "shape": "scalar",
    "symbol": "$$Z$$",
    "meaning": "Total minimized cost over the planning horizon"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "time_horizon": 4,
  "demand": [15, 25, 35, 25],
  "capacity": [30, 40, 45, 20],
  "production_cost": [5.0, 5.1, 5.4, 5.5],
  "holding_cost": 0.2,
  "initial_inventory": 0
}
